  cargo test -p object-storage --lib -- --exact client::tests::presign_rejects_out_of_range_expiry_without_calling_the_provider
    restricted file-access sandbox : panicked - TrustStore configured to enable native roots but no valid root certificates parsed!
    normal file access (same binary): passed
  => the panic depends on the execution environment's ability to read the OS root certificate
     store, not on repository code. Source of the panic: aws-smithy-runtime's rustls provider
     (aws-smithy-http-client rustls provider: debug_assert! after rustls_native_certs::load_native_certs()
     yields zero roots; the root set is a LazyLock, so it is loaded once per process).

DECISION: treated as an execution-environment difference. Production TLS verification is
unchanged; the parameter-rejection unit tests no longer construct an SDK client with the
default HTTPS connector at all - they install a no-network transport (src/client.rs
tests::offline_client), so they never read the host trust store.

